# The manifest pins SHA-256 of the bytes raw.githubusercontent serves, which are
# always LF. Without this, git checks out CRLF working copies, sync-from-potassium
# hashes THOSE, and every user fails verification on any file the sync did not
# freshly copy from the canonical repo. gate.ps1 cannot catch it: it hashes the
# same working copy the sync did.
* -text
*.lua text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
